From e4b7e17ed965a5166d56ecfdc2967b34082a74c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: proshiv85-byte <proshiv85@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:01:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/25] WIP: Exynos8895 PCIe host + BCM4361 WiFi

New pcie-exynos8895 DWC glue: PHY/reset sequence from the vendor kernel,
WLAN_REG_ON as vpcie3v3 regulator, PERST# via reset-gpios, INTx only.
The 4 MiB outbound window cannot hold the 4 MiB TCM BAR plus the
register BAR, so an oversized BAR is clipped to a prefetchable window
and the rest is translated to bus addresses above its decode range
(the vendor kernel ends up with the same layout).

brcmfmac: BCM4361 (14e4:441f) ids, RAM base, firmware entry with the
random seed. Works with Samsung's 13.38.64 B0 firmware.

DT: PCIe channel 0 on the dream2lte, WLAN enable regulator and pins.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
---
